-dir`/`--work-tree`), so a pointer rewritten after the check is not re-read; `nestedRepositoryReason` refuses gitlinks (a path may contain any character, a newline included) and untracked directories that hold a planted repository at any depth, and receipt certification runs it before any Git is run inside a submodule; a gitlink or directory whose name is not valid UTF-8 cannot be matched on disk, so it is refused rather than skipped (an ordinary file with such a name is fine) (untracked directories are searched on disk within a budget, ignored directories are skipped, and exceeding the budget refuses) and is used by `statusOf`, `hasChangesAt`, `worktree remove` and the session helpers. The session helpers (`cli/src/git.ts`: status badge, `/commit`) and the checkpoint manager refuse the same worktrees; status, branch and `/commit` also run against the verified directory, checkpoint internals only check. `getGitInfo` reports the refusal instead of "not a repository". The real repository's own signing and filter configuration is the operator's and is not pinned. Merge (receipt, waiver or neither), `remove` and `prune` refuse a worktree holding a modification that Git's index or configuration hides (`--assume-unchanged`, `--skip-worktree`, `core.fileMode=false`): the strict snapshot must equal the tree a merge would commit (`hiddenModificationReason`; `remove --force` discards knowingly). The session's `/diff`, `/copy diff`, `/stage` and the REPL `git diff` run against the verified directory too. Open residuals: checkpoint internals and `copy-ignored` check but do not pin; a submodule's own `.git` swapped after `nestedRepositoryReason`; `git worktree remove` without `--force` runs its own `git status` child that re-reads `.git` after the pre-removal verification (`--force` would skip Git's own submodule safety); task-worktree merge, discard and ignored-output paths in `cli/src/worktree.ts` and other Git calls from before this stack still run plain Git. (2) A clean source whose index differs from HEAD refuses the merge (this replaces the earlier unstage-before-squash and `--only` guards). (3) The target checkout's branch is re-read right before the fast-forward. (4) Renamed `unrecordableWorktree`. (5) The test passes the waiver directly. (6) `cleanReply` drops trailer-shaped lines from the body (Git's trailer grammar: `Key: v`, `Key:v`, `Key : v`, `Key #n`, `BREAKING CHANGE`; legitimate prose such as `Note: ...` goes too); a file name with control, C1 or bidi-override characters no longer reaches the deterministic message, and such a model reply is unusable. Refusal messages show control bytes from agent-controlled paths escaped, and a repository-controlled project `.env` is read only as a small regular file (a symlink to one is followed; a FIFO, device or oversized file is skipped with a warning, so it cannot hang the host); the refusal messages (worktree helper, session helpers, checkpoint manager), Git's own error line and the merge notes that print Git output or submodule names are shown with control, C1, bidi and line-separator characters escaped (paths printed through `shownPath` come from the operator's own repository layout); `merge --ai-message` builds its provider configuration without the project `.env` layer, since the process runs inside the agent-writable worktree, and a session's `/worktree merge --ai-message` sends nothing to an endpoint a project `.env` chose; a session (configured or discovered verifier) that starts in a linked worktree holding uncommitted work, one that cannot be certified, or one whose `.git` is missing or replaced (judged once per workspace, where the session starts, so its own later verified work does not count) verifies as usual but issues no receipt on that baseline (`receiptBaselineUntrusted`; such a merge needs the waiver), because the agent may have rewritten the tests and verifier files in an earlier session. A failing waiver write after the fast-forward is a note, and one shared `parseSubmoduleStatus` handles paths with spaces; `cli/test/worktrunk_trust.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_sibling_layout.test.ts`, `cli/test/worktrunk_ai_message.test.ts` |
